{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-6a-15-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "6a:15", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.6a.15", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.6a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תָּא שְׁמַע: בְּהֵמָה טְהוֹרָה שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין בְּהֵמָה טְמֵאָה — פְּטוּרָה מִן הַבְּכוֹרָה, אִם יֵשׁ בּוֹ מִקְצָת סִימָנִין — חַיֶּיבֶת בִּבְכוֹרָה. מַאי לָאו אֲפִילּוּ פָּרָה שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין סוּס? לֹא, פָּרָה שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין חֲמוֹר.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Bekhorot 6a:15. A baraita is tested against the case of cow or donkey producing horse-like young; the discussion concerns firstborn liability and partial identifying signs.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A baraita is tested against the case of cow or donkey producing horse-like young; the discussion concerns firstborn liability and partial identifying signs.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "horse_like_offspring_hypothetical", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-6a-16-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "6a:16", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.6a.16", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.6a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תָּא שְׁמַע: פָּרָה שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין חֲמוֹר, וַחֲמוֹר שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין סוּס — פְּטוּרָה מִן הַבְּכוֹרָה, אִם יֵשׁ בּוֹ מִקְצָת סִימָנִין — חַיֶּיבֶת בִּבְכוֹרָה. מַאי לָאו אַתַּרְוַיְיהוּ? לָא, אַפָּרָה שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין חֲמוֹר.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Bekhorot 6a:16. The baraita distinguishes horse-like appearance from partial maternal-species signs when determining firstborn liability.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The baraita distinguishes horse-like appearance from partial maternal-species signs when determining firstborn liability.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "horse_like_offspring_hypothetical", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-6a-17-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "6a:17", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.6a.17", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.6a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אֲבָל חֲמוֹר שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין סוּס, לְמַאי קָתָנֵי לַהּ? לִפְטוּרָא? פְּשִׁיטָא! הַשְׁתָּא, וּמָה פָּרָה שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין חֲמוֹר, דְּאִידֵּי וְאִידֵּי בְּנֵי מִיקְדָּשׁ בִּבְכוֹרָה נִינְהוּ, אָמְרַתְּ: אִם יֵשׁ בּוֹ מִקְצָת סִימָנִין — אִין, וְאִי לָא — לָא, חֲמוֹר שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין סוּס מִיבַּעְיָא?", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Bekhorot 6a:17. The sugya explains why donkey bearing horse-like young is not redundant, comparing horns and split or unsplit hooves; it is legal morphology.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The sugya explains why donkey bearing horse-like young is not redundant, comparing horns and split or unsplit hooves; it is legal morphology.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "horse_like_offspring_hypothetical", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-7a-23-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "7a:23", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.7a.23", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.7a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "וְתִיבְּעֵי לֵיהּ דְּסוּסִים וּגְמַלִּים? דְּסוּסִים וּגְמַלִּים לָא מִיבַּעְיָא לְהוּ, דְּלָא עֲכִירִי וְלָא דָּמוּ לְחָלָב, מַיָּא עוּל מַיָּא נְפוּק. כִּי קָמִיבַּעְיָא לְהוּ דַּחֲמוֹר, דַּעֲכִירִי וְדָמוּ לְחָלָב, מַאי? מִגּוּפֵיהּ קָא מִימַּצְצִי וַאֲסִירִי, אוֹ דִלְמָא מַיָּא עוּל מַיָּא נְפוּק, וְהַאי דַּעֲכִירִי — הַבְלָא דְּבִישְׂרָא הוּא?", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Bekhorot 7a:23. Horse and camel urine are contrasted with cloudy donkey urine in a food-law inquiry; the stated rationale is that clear urine resembles ingested and excreted water.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Horse and camel urine are contrasted with cloudy donkey urine in a food-law inquiry; the stated rationale is that clear urine resembles ingested and excreted water.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "horse_urine_status", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-7b-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "7b:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.7b.2", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.7b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "וְאִיכָּא דְּאָמְרִי, דְּסוּסִים וּגְמַלִּים לָא קָא מִיבַּעְיָא לְהוּ, דְּלָא שָׁתוּ אִינָשֵׁי. כִּי קָמִיבַּעְיָא לְהוּ דַּחֲמוֹר, דְּשָׁתוּ אִינָשֵׁי וּמְעַלּוּ לְיַרְקוֹנָא, מַאי?", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Bekhorot 7b:2. An alternative formulation excludes horse and camel urine from the practical question because people do not drink it; the live question concerns donkey urine used for jaundice.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "An alternative formulation excludes horse and camel urine from the practical question because people do not drink it; the live question concerns donkey urine used for jaundice.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "horse_urine_status", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-40a-14-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "40a:14", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.40a.14", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.40a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "וְהַשָּׁחוּל וְהַכָּסוּל וְכוּ׳. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: אֵיזֶהוּ כָּסוּל וְאֵיזֶהוּ שָׁחוּל? שָׁחוּל — שֶׁנִּשְׁמְטָה יְרֵיכוֹ, כָּסוּל — שֶׁרַגְלוֹ אֶחָד בְּתוֹךְ הַכֶּסֶל, וְרַגְלוֹ אֶחָד עַל גַּבֵּי הַכֶּסֶל. תָּנָא: הַשָּׂרוּעַ וְהַקָּלוּט — שָׂרוּעַ שֶׁנִּשְׁתַּרְבֵּב לוֹ יְרֵיכוֹ, קָלוּט — שֶׁרַגְלָיו קְלוּטוֹת כְּשֶׁל חֲמוֹר וּכְשֶׁל סוּס.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Bekhorot 40a:14. A fused hoof like that of a donkey or horse defines the bodily defect קָלוּט in a firstborn-animal discussion.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A fused hoof like that of a donkey or horse defines the bodily defect קָלוּט in a firstborn-animal discussion.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "horse_hoof_comparison", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chagigah-9b-12-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chagigah", "locator": "9b:12", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah.9b.12", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Chagigah.9b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אֲמַר לֵיהּ אֵלִיָּהוּ לְבַר הֵי הֵי, וְאָמְרִי לַהּ לְרַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר: מַאי דִּכְתִיב: ״הִנֵּה צְרַפְתִּיךָ וְלֹא בְכָסֶף בְּחַרְתִּיךָ בְּכוּר עוֹנִי״ — מְלַמֵּד שֶׁחָזַר הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא עַל כׇּל מִדּוֹת טוֹבוֹת לִיתֵּן לְיִשְׂרָאֵל, וְלֹא מָצָא אֶלָּא עֲנִיּוּת. אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל וְאִיתֵּימָא רַב יוֹסֵף, הַיְינוּ דְּאָמְרִי אִינָשֵׁי: יָאָה עַנְיוּתָא לִיהוּדָאֵי כִּי בַּרְזָא סוּמָּקָא לְסוּסְיָא חִיוָּרָא.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Chagigah 9b:12. A proverb says poverty suits Jews like a red strap on a white horse; the horse supplies a visual comparison, not supernatural symbolism.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A proverb says poverty suits Jews like a red strap on a white horse; the horse supplies a visual comparison, not supernatural symbolism.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "white_horse_proverb", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chullin-5a-1-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chullin", "locator": "5a:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.5a.1", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Chullin.5a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "לָא הֲוָה מְפַלֵּיג נַפְשֵׁיהּ מִינֵּיהּ, מְנָלַן? אִילֵּימָא מִדִּכְתִיב ״כָּמוֹנִי כָמוֹךָ כְּעַמִּי כְעַמֶּךָ״, אֶלָּא מֵעַתָּה ״כְּסוּסַי כְּסוּסֶיךָ״ הָכִי נָמֵי? אֶלָּא מָה דְּהָוֵי אַסּוּסֶיךָ תֶּהֱוֵי אַסּוּסַי, הָכִי נָמֵי מַאי דְּהָוֵי עֲלָךְ וְעִילָּוֵי עַמָּךְ תֶּיהֱוֵי עֲלַי וְעִילָּוֵי עַמִּי.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Chullin 5a:1. The verse 'my horses as your horses' is parsed as shared military fate, in an argument about Jehoshaphat’s association with Ahab; the horses are ordinary royal forces.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The verse 'my horses as your horses' is parsed as shared military fate, in an argument about Jehoshaphat’s association with Ahab; the horses are ordinary royal forces.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "royal_horse_equivalence", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chullin-79a-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chullin", "locator": "79a:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.79a.2", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Chullin.79a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר רַב הוּנָא בַּר חִיָּיא אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: הִלְכְתָא כַּחֲנַנְיָה, וְאַזְדָּא שְׁמוּאֵל לְטַעְמֵיהּ, דִּתְנַן: רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: הַנּוֹלָדִים מִן הַסּוּס, אַף עַל פִּי שֶׁאֲבִיהֶן חֲמוֹר – מוּתָּרִין זֶה בְּזֶה, אֲבָל הַנּוֹלָדִין מִן הַחֲמוֹר עִם הַנּוֹלָדִין מִן הַסּוּס – אֲסוּרִין.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Chullin 79a:2. A dispute over paternal lineage classifies mule offspring by horse or donkey maternity and asks which pairings count as one kind.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A dispute over paternal lineage classifies mule offspring by horse or donkey maternity and asks which pairings count as one kind.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "mule_parentage", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chullin-79a-4-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chullin", "locator": "79a:4", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.79a.4", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Chullin.79a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַאן חֲכָמִים? חֲנַנְיָה הוּא, דְּאָמַר חוֹשְׁשִׁין לְזֶרַע הָאָב, וְהַאי בַּר סוּסְיָא וַחֲמָרָא, וְהַאי בַּר חֲמָרָא וְסוּסְיָא – כּוּלְּהוּ חֲדָא מִינָא נִינְהוּ.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Chullin 79a:4. The sugya identifies the Sages with Hananiah and treats horse-donkey and donkey-horse parentage as one mule kind under his view.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The sugya identifies the Sages with Hananiah and treats horse-donkey and donkey-horse parentage as one mule kind under his view.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "mule_parentage", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chullin-79a-7-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chullin", "locator": "79a:7", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.79a.7", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Chullin.79a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַאי תָּא שְׁמַע: רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: כׇּל הַנּוֹלָדִים מִן הַסּוּס, אַף עַל פִּי שֶׁאֲבִיהֶן חֲמוֹר – מוּתָּרִין זֶה בָּזֶה. הֵיכִי דָמֵי? אִילֵּימָא דַּאֲבוּהּ דְּהַאי חֲמוֹר וַאֲבוּהּ דְּהַאי חֲמוֹר – צְרִיכָא לְמֵימַר? אֶלָּא לָאו דַּאֲבוּהּ דְּהַאי סוּס וַאֲבוּהּ דְּהַאי חֲמוֹר;", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Chullin 79a:7. A proof attempt tests whether R. Judah disregards paternal seed by comparing offspring of mares sired by horses or donkeys.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A proof attempt tests whether R. Judah disregards paternal seed by comparing offspring of mares sired by horses or donkeys.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "mule_parentage", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chullin-79a-9-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chullin", "locator": "79a:9", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.79a.9", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Chullin.79a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "לָא, לְעוֹלָם דַּאֲבוּהּ דְּהַאי חֲמוֹר, וַאֲבוּהּ דְּהַאי חֲמוֹר. וּדְקָאָמְרַתְּ: צְרִיכָא לְמֵימַר? מַהוּ דְּתֵימָא: אָתֵי צַד דְּסוּס מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בְּצַד חֲמוֹר, וְצַד חֲמוֹר מִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ בְּצַד סוּס, קָא מַשְׁמַע לַן.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Chullin 79a:9. The proof is rejected by reading both fathers as donkeys; 'horse side' and 'donkey side' describe mixed ancestry relevant to prohibited labor pairings.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The proof is rejected by reading both fathers as donkeys; 'horse side' and 'donkey side' describe mixed ancestry relevant to prohibited labor pairings.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "mule_parentage", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-chullin-79a-10-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Chullin", "locator": "79a:10", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.79a.10", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Chullin.79a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תָּא שְׁמַע: רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר, פִּרְדָּה שֶׁתָּבְעָה – אֵין מַרְבִּיעִין עָלֶיהָ לֹא סוּס וְלֹא חֲמוֹר, אֶלָּא מִינָהּ. וְאִי אָמְרַתְּ מִפְשָׁט פְּשִׁיטָא לֵיהּ לַרְבַּע עֲלַהּ מִינָא דְּאִמַּהּ! דְּלָא יָדְעִינַן מִינָא דְּאִמַּהּ מַאי נִיהוּ.", "context": "Read the target and up to two adjacent segments on Chullin 79a:10. R. Judah forbids mating a female mule with either horse or donkey when its maternal kind is unknown; voice, ears and tail are proposed as lineage signs.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Judah forbids mating a female mule with either horse or donkey when its maternal kind is unknown; voice, ears and tail are proposed as lineage signs.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["coordinator-2026-10-11"], "task_id": "BAV-006", "role": "mule_breeding_identification", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review.", "Legal and proverbial claims are retained as attributed discourse, not external historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-shabbat-6-1-3-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Shabbat", "locator": "6:1:3", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Shabbat.6.1.3", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Moed/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "indirect", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "רִבִּי זְעִירָא בָעֵי. קָשַׁר נֵימָא לַחֲבֵירָתָהּ. אַחַת הִיא. אַחַת לִשְׁתַּיִם שְׁתַּיִם הֵן. לְשָׁלֹֹש שָׁלֹשׁ הֵן. רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר. זוֹ שֶׁהִיא יוֹרֶדֶת לִטְבּוֹל לְנִידָּתָהּ קוֹשֶׁרֶת שְׂעָרָהּ כִּזְנָב הַסּוּס. לְעוּבְרָה וּסְמִיךְ עֲלֹי.", "context": "Complete segment asks about tying strands and reports Rav Judah's practical ruling: a woman descending to immerse ties her hair like a horse's tail. Ordinary horse-tail simile; no supernatural movement.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment asks about tying strands and reports Rav Judah's practical ruling: a woman descending to immerse ties her hair like a horse's tail. Ordinary horse-tail simile; no supernatural movement.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "YER-007", "role": "horse_tail_hair_simile", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-shabbat-8-2-3-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Shabbat", "locator": "8:2:3", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Shabbat.8.2.3", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Moed/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Shabbat/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "indirect", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "גֶּמִי כְּדֵי לַעֲשׂוֹת תְּלוּי לְנָפָה וְלִכְבָרָה. הָדָא דָאַתְּ אָמַר בָּהֵין גַּוַויָא. בְּרֵם בָּהֶן בַּרַיָיא כְּדֵי לַעֲשׂוֹת שְׁנֵי בָתִּים לְנָפָה וְלִכְבָרָה. תַּנֵּי. הוּצִּין כְּדֵי לַעֲשׂוֹת אוֹזֶן לִקְפִיפָה מִצְרִית. הָדָא דְאַתְּ אָמַר בְּאִילֵּין רַכִּיכַיָּא. בְּרַם בָּאִילֵּין קַשִּׁיָיא כְּדֵי לַעֲשׂוֹת צְפוֹרָה. הוֹצִיא כְלֵי נְצָרִים חַיָיב. תּוֹרֵי דֶקֶל שְׁנַיִם. זְמוֹרוֹת לִנְטִיעָה שְׁתַּיִם. אִם לִבְהֵמָה כִּמְלוֹא פִי גְדִי. אִם לָעֵצִים כְּשִׁיעוּר הָעֵצִים. הוֹצִיא שְׁתֵּי נִימִין מִזְּנַב הַסּוּס מִזְּנַב הַפָּרָה חַיָיב. שֶׁכֵּן מַתְקִינִין אוֹתָן לַנִּשְׁבִּין. זִיפֵי חֲזִיר. אִית תַּנָּיֵי תַנֵּי. שְׁתַּיִם. אִית תַּנָּיֵי תַנֵּי. אַחַת. מָאן דְּאָמַר. שְׁתַּיִם. בְּאִילֵּין רַכִּיכָתָא. מָאן דְּאָמַר. אַחַת. בָּאִילֵּין קַשִּׁיָיתָא. גַּלָעִינִים לִנְטִיעָה שְׁתַּיִם. אִם לִבְהֵמָה כִּמְלוֹא פִי חֲזִיר. כַּמָּה הוּא מְלֹא פִיו. אַחַת. אֲחֵרִים אוֹמְרִים. חֶשְׁבּוֹן חָמֵשׁ. הוֹצִיא סִיאָה אֵזוּב וְקוּרְנִית. אִם לָאוֹכְלִין כִּגְרוֹגֶרֶת. אִם לִבְהֵמָה כִּמְלוֹא פִי גְדִי. אִם לָעֵצִים כְּשִׁיעוּר הָעֵצִים. אִם לְהַזָּיָיה כְשִׁיעוּר הַזָּיָיה.", "context": "Complete segment sets Sabbath carrying quantities for plant and animal materials. Two hairs from a horse's or cow's tail are liable because they are prepared for traps. Material-use rule, not a horse narrative.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment sets Sabbath carrying quantities for plant and animal materials. Two hairs from a horse's or cow's tail are liable because they are prepared for traps. Material-use rule, not a horse narrative.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "YER-007", "role": "horse_tail_hair_material", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-shekalim-7-2-6-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Shekalim", "locator": "7:2:6", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Shekalim.7.2.6", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Moed/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Shekalim/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר רִבִּי יוֹחָנָן. הַנִּמְצָא בְיַד גּוֹי כְּנִמְצָא בַפַּלַּטְיָא. רִבִּי לָעְזָר בֵּירִבִּי חַגַּיי הֲוָה מְסַמֵּךְ לְרִבִּי מָנָא. חֲמָא לְחַד אֲרָמַאי מְקַטֵּעַ מִן סוּסֵיהּ וּמַפִּיק לִבְרָא. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. הָדָא הִיא דְאָמַר רִבִּי יוֹחָנָן. הַנִּמְצָא בְיַד גּוֹי כְּנִמְצָא בַפַּלַּטְיָא. אָמַר לֵיהּ. כֵּן אָמַר רִבִּי יוֹסֵי רִבִּי. וְהֵן שֶׂרָאוּ אוֹתוֹ יוֹצֵא מִמַּקֻּילִין שֶׁל יִשְׂרָאֵל. חַד בַּר נַשׁ בְּצִיפּוֹרִין אֲזַל בָּעֵי מִיזְבוֹן קוּפָּד מִן טַבְּחָא וְלָא יְהַב לֵיהּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ לְחַד רוֹמַיי וְאַיְיתִי לֵיהּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. לָא נָסְבִּית עַל כָּרְחֵיהּ. אֲמַר. וְלָאו בְּשַׂר דִּנְבֵילָה יְהָבִית לֵיהּ. רִבִּי יִרְמְיָה בְשֵׁם רִבִּי חֲנִינָה. מַעֲשֶׂה בָא לִפְנֵי רִבִּי וְאָמַר. לָא כוּלָּא מִינֵּיהּ מֵיסּוֹר מַקֻּילִין דְּצִיפּוֹרִין.", "context": "Complete segment discusses the status of meat found in a non-Jew's possession. R. Eleazar b. Haggai sees a non-Jew cutting from his horse and taking it outside; the episode illustrates R. Johanan's rule and is qualified by R. Yose's report. Ordinary animal/meat context, not supernatural movement.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment discusses the status of meat found in a non-Jew's possession. R. Eleazar b. Haggai sees a non-Jew cutting from his horse and taking it outside; the episode illustrates R. Johanan's rule and is qualified by R. Yose's report. Ordinary animal/meat context, not supernatural movement.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "YER-007", "role": "horse_as_source_of_meat", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-sotah-5-4-3-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Sotah", "locator": "5:4:3", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Sotah.5.4.3", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Nashim/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Sotah/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַה תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר לֵאמֹר. לֵאמֹר לְדוֹרוֹת. רִבִּי אַבָּהוּ בְשֵׁם רִבִּי יוֹסֵי בֵּירִבִּי חֲנִינָה. כְּהָדֵין פְּסוּקָא. מֹֹשֶׁה אָמַר אָשִׁירָה. וְהֵן עוֹנִין אַחֲרָיו אָשִׁירָה לַיי כִּי גָאֹה גָּאָה סוּס וְרוֹכְבוֹ רָמָה בַיָּם. מֹשֶׁה אָמַר עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת וְהֵן עוֹנִין אַחֲרָיו עָזִּי וְזִמְרָת יָ׳הּ. כְּתִיב בִּפְרוֹעַ פְּרָעוֹת בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל בְּהִתְנַדֵּב עָם. הִתְנַדְּבוּ רָאשֵׁי עָם. כְּשֶׁהַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא עוֹשֶׂה לָהֶן נִיסִּים יְהוּ אוֹמְרִים שִׁירָה. הָתִיבוּן. הֲרֵי גְּאוּלַּת מִצְרַיִם. שַׁנְיָיא הִיא שֶׁהִיא תְּחִילַּת גְּאוּלָּתָן. הָתִיבוּן. הֲרֵי גְּאוּלַּת מָרְדֳּכַי וְאֶסְתֵּר. שַׁנְיָיא הִיא. שֶׁהָיוּ בְחוּצָה לָאָרֶץ. וְאִית דְּבָעֵי מֵימַר. מָרְדֳּכָי וְאֶסְתֵּר מְשּׂוֹנְאֵיהֶן נִגְאֲלוּ. לֹא נִגְאֲלוּ מִן הַמַּלְכוּת.", "context": "Complete segment explains responsive recitation of the Song at the Sea and quotes 'horse and its rider He cast into the sea.' Biblical liturgical quotation about divine deliverance, not horse-powered supernatural travel.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment explains responsive recitation of the Song at the Sea and quotes 'horse and its rider He cast into the sea.' Biblical liturgical quotation about divine deliverance, not horse-powered supernatural travel.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "YER-008", "role": "song_at_sea_horse_and_rider", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-taanit-4-5-13-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Taanit", "locator": "4:5:13", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Taanit.4.5.13", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Moed/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Taanit/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תַּנֵּי רִבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן יוֹחַי. עֲקִיבָה רִבִּי הָיָה דוֹרֵשׁ דָּרַךְ כּוֹכָב מִיַּעֲקֹב. דָּרַךְ כּוֹזִבָּא מִיַּעֲקֹב. רִבִּי עֲקִיבָה כַּד הֲוָה חֲמִי בַּר כּוֹזִבָּה הֲוָה אֲמַר. דֵּין הוּא מַלְכָּא מְשִׁיחָא. אָמַר לֵיהּ רִבִּי יוֹחָנָן בֵּן תּוֹרְתָא. עֲקִיבָה. יַעֲלוּ עֲשָׂבִים בִּלְחָיֵיךָ (וְאַדַּיִין) [וְעַדַּיִין] בֶּן דָּוִד [לֹא] יָבֹא. אָמַר רִבִּי יוֹחָנָן. קוֹל אַדְרִיָינוּס קַיְסָר הוֹרֵג בְּבֵיתְתָּר שְׁמוֹנִים אֶלֶף רִיבּוֹא. אָמַר רִבִּי יוֹחָנָן. שְׁמוֹנִים [אֶלֶף] זוּג שֶׁלְתוֹקְעֵי קְרָנוֹת הָיוּ מַקִּיפִין אֶת בֵּיתְתָּר. וְכָל אֶחָד וְאֶחָד הָיָה מְמוּנֶּה עַל כַּמָּה חַיָילוֹת. וְהָיָה שָׁם בֶּן כּוֹזִבָּה וְהָיָה לֹו מָאתַיִם אֶלֶף מְטִיפֵי אֶצְבַּע. שָׁלְחוּ חֲכָמִים וְאָמְרוּ לוֹ. עַד אֵימָתַי אַתָּה עוֹשֶׂה אֶת יִשְׂרָאֵל בַּעֲלֵי מוּמִין. אָמַר לָהֶן. וְכִי הֵיאַךְ אֶיפְשַׁר לְבוֹדְקָן. אָמְרוּ לוֹ. כָּל מִי שֶׁאֵינוֹ רוֹכֵב עַל סוּסוֹ וְעוֹקֵר אֶרֶז מִן לְבָנוֹן לָא יִהיֶה נִכְתָּב בְּאִיסְרַטְיָא שֵּׁלָּךְ. וְהָיוּ לוֹ מָאתַיִם אֶלֶף כָּךְ וּמָאתַיִם אֶלֶף כָּךְ. וְכַד דַּהֲוָה נְפַק לִקְרָבָא הֲוָה אֲמַר. רִיבּוֹנֵיהּ דְּעָלְמָא. לֹא תִסְעוֹד וְלֹא תִ[כְסוֹף]. הֲלֹא אַתָּה אֱלֹהִים זְנַחְתָּנוּ וְלֹא תֵצֵא בְּצִבְאוֹתֵינוּ. שָׁלֹשׁ שָׁנִים וּמֶחֱצָה עָשָׂה אַדְרִיָינוּס מַקִּיף עַל בֵּיתְתָּר. וַהֲוָה רִבִּי אֶלְעָזָר הַמּוֹדָעִי יוֹשֵׁב עַל הַשַּׂק וְעַל הָאֶפֶר וּמִתְפַּלֵּל בְּכָל יוֹם וְאוֹמֵר. רִבּוֹן הָעוֹלָמִים. אַל תֵּשֵׁב בַּדִּין הַיּוֹם. אַל תֵּשֵׁב בַּדִּין הַיּוֹם. בְּעָא אַדְרִיָינוּס מֵיזַל לֵיהּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ חַד כּותַיי. לָא תֵיזִיל לָךְ. דַּאֲנָא חֲמִי מַה מֵיעֲבַד וּמַשְׁלִים לָךְ מְדִינְתָא. עָאַל לֵיהּ מִן בַּיְבָא דִמְדִינִתָא. עָאַל וְאַשְׁכָּח רִבִּי אֶלְעָזָר הַמּוֹדָעִי קָאִים מַצְלִי. עֲבַד נַפְשֵׁיהּ לְחִישׁ לֵיהּ בְּגַו אוּדְנֵיהּ. חֶמוּנֵיהּ בְּנֵי מְדִינְתָא וְאַיְיתוּנֵיהּ גַּבֵּי בֶּן כוֹזִבָּא. אָמְרוּן לֵיהּ. חֲמִינָן הָהֵן סַבָּא מִשְׁתָּעֵי לַחֲבִיבָךְ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. מַה אָמְרָת לֵיהּ וּמַה אֲמַר לָךְ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. [אִין] אֲנָא אֲמַר לָךְ מַלְכָּא קְטַל לִי. וְאִי לָא אֲנָא אֲמַר לָךְ אַתְּ קְטַל יָתִי. טַב לִי מַלְכָּא קְטַל יָתִי וְלָא אַתְּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. אֲמַר לִי דַאֲנָא מַשְׁלִים מְדִינְתָא. אֲתַא גַּבֵּי רִבִּי אֶלְעָזָר הַמּוֹדָעִי. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. מַה אֲמַר לָךְ הָדֵין כּוּתַיָיא. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. לֹא כְלוּם. מָה אָמְרָת לֵיהּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. לֹא כְלוּם. יְהַב לֵיהּ חַד בְּעוּט וְקָטְלֵיהּ. מִיַּד יָצָאת בַּת קוֹל וְאָמְרָה. הוֹי רוֹעִי הָאֱלִיל עוֹזְבִי הַצֹּאן חֶרֶב עַל זְרוֹעוֹ וְעַל עֵין יְמִינוֹ זְרוֹעוֹ יָבֹשׁ תִּיבָשׁ וְעֵין יְמִינוֹ כָּהֹה תִכְהֶה. הָרַגְתָּ אֶת רִבִּי אֶלְעָזָר הַמּוֹדָעִי זְרוֹעָן שֶׁלכָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל וְעֵין יְמִינָם. לְפִיכָךְ זְרוֹעוֹ שֶׁלְאוֹתוֹ הָאִישׁ יָבוֹשׁ תִּיבָשׁ וְעֵין יְמִינוֹ כָּהֹה תִכְהֶה. מִיַּד נִלְכְּדָה בֵיתָתָּר וְנֶהֱרַג בֶּן כּוֹזִבָּה. אַתּוֹן טְעִינִין רִישֵׁיהּ גַּבֵּי אַדְרִיָינוּס. אֲמַר לוֹן. מָאן קְטַל הָדֵין. אֲמַר לֵיהּ חַד כּוּתַיָיא. אֲנָא קְטַלְתֵּיהּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. חֲמִי לִי פִטוּמֵיהּ. חֲמִי לֵיהּ פִטוּמֵיהּ. אַשְׁכַּח חֲכִינָה כִרִיכָה עֲלוֹי. אֲמַר. אִלוּלֵי אֱלָהָא דְקָטְלֵיהּ מָאן הֲוָה יְכִיל קָטְלֵיהּ. וְקָרָא עֲלוֹי. אִם לֹא כִּי צוּרָם מְכָרָם וַיי הִסְגִּרָם. וְהָיוּ הוֹרֵגִין בָּהֶם וְהוֹלְכִין עַד שֶׁשָּׁקַע הַסּוּס בָּדָם עַד חוֹטְמוֹ. וְהָיָה הַדָּם מְגַלְגֵּל סְלָעִים מַשְּׂאוּי אַרְבָּעִים סְאָה עַד שֶׁהָלַךְ הַדָּם בַּיָּם אַרְבָּעַת מִיל. אִם תֹאמַר שֶׁהִיא קְרוֹבָה לַיָּם. וַהֲלֹא רְחוֹקָה מִן הַיָּם אַרְבָּעִים מִיל. אָמְרוּ. שְׁלֹשׁ מֵאוֹת מוֹחֵי תִינּוֹקוֹת מָצְאוּ עַל אֶבֶן אַחַת. וּמָצְאוּ שָׁלֹשׁ קוּפּוֹת שֶׁלְקְצוּצֵי תְפִילִּין שֶׁלְתֵּשַׁע תֵּשַׁע סְאִין. וְיֵשׁ אוֹמְרִים. תֵּשַׁע שֶׁל שָׁלֹשׁ שָׁלֹשׁ סְאִין. תַּנֵּי. רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֵּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר. חֲמֵשׁ מֵאוֹת בָּתֵּי סוֹפְרִים הָיוּ בְּבֵיתְתָּר. וְהַקָּטָן שֶׁבָּהֶן אֵין פָּחוּת מֵחֲמֵשׁ מֵאוֹת תִּינוֹקוֹת. וְהָיוּ אוֹמְרִים. אִם בָּאוּ הַשּׂוֹנְאִים עָלֵינוּ בַּמַּכְתּוֹבִים הַלָּלוּ אָנוּ יוֹצְאִין עֲלֵיהֶן וּמְנַקְּרִים אֶת עֵינֵיהֶם. וְכֵיוָן שֶׁגָּרְמוּ עֲוֹנוֹת הָיוּ כוֹרְכִים כָּל אֶחָד וְאֶחָד בְּסִפְרוֹ וְשׂוֹרְפִין אוֹתוֹ. וּמִכּוּלָּם לָא נִשְׁתַּיֵיר אֶלָא אָנִי. וְקָרָא עַל גַּרְמֵיהּ. עֵינִי עוֹלְלָה לְנַפְשִׁי מִכֹּל בְּנוֹת עִירִי. כֶּרֶם גָּדוֹל הָיָה לְאַדְרִיָינוּס הָרָשָׁע. שְׁמוֹנֶה עָשָׂר מִיל עַל שְׁמוֹנֶה עָשָׂר מִיל כְּמִין טִיבֵּרִיְּא לְצִיפּוֹרִי. וְהִקִּיפוֹ גָּדֵר מֵהָרוּגֵי בֵּיתְתָּר מְלֹא קוֹמָה וּפִישּׁוּט יָדַיִים. וְלֹא גָזַר עֲלֵיהֶם שְׁיִּיקָבֵרוּ. עַד שֶׁעָמַד מֶלֶךְ אַחֵר וְגָזַר עֲלֵיהֶם שְׁיִּיקָבֵרוּ.", "context": "Complete segment narrates Bar Koziva and the fall of Betar. Mounted uprooting of a cedar is a military strength test; a horse later sinking to its nostrils in blood is atrocity/hyperbole imagery. Extraordinary scale, but no flying or interworld horse.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment narrates Bar Koziva and the fall of Betar. Mounted uprooting of a cedar is a military strength test; a horse later sinking to its nostrils in blood is atrocity/hyperbole imagery. Extraordinary scale, but no flying or interworld horse.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "YER-008", "role": "betar_war_horses", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "a