{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-gittin-14b-5-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Gittin", "locator": "14b:5", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Gittin.14b.5", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Nashim/Gittin/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אמר ליה: בני אדם הללו קרובים למלכות הן? אמר ליה: הן. יש להן סוסים ופרדים שרצים אחריהן? אמר ליה: הן. אמר ליה: אי הכי, שפיר עבדת.", "context": "The presence of fast-following horses and mules establishes that certain people are close to the government and capable of pursuit; ordinary status and enforcement capacity.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "The presence of fast-following horses and mules establishes that certain people are close to the government and capable of pursuit; ordinary status and enforcement capacity.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horses_as_status_and_pursuit_capacity", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-ketubot-66a-5-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Ketubot", "locator": "66a:5", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot.66a.5", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Nashim/Ketubot/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "בושתה ופגמה. מתקיף לה רבא בר רב חנן: אלא מעתה, בייש סוסתו של חבירו, הכי נמי דבעי למיתן ליה בושת? וסוס בר בושת הוא?! אלא: רקק בבגדו של חבירו, הכי נמי דבעי למיתן ליה בושת?", "context": "Rava tests a theory of compensation for humiliation by asking whether embarrassing another person’s horse would incur humiliation damages, then rejects the category because a horse is not subject to shame.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Rava tests a theory of compensation for humiliation by asking whether embarrassing another person’s horse would incur humiliation damages, then rejects the category because a horse is not subject to shame.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_in_damages_analogy", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-ketubot-67a-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Ketubot", "locator": "67a:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot.67a.2", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Nashim/Ketubot/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תניא: אמר רבי אלעזר ברבי צדוק: אראה בנחמה, אם לא ראיתיה שהיתה מלקטת שעורים מבין טלפי סוסים בעכו. קראתי עליה מקרא זה: ״אם לא תדעי לך היפה בנשים צאי לך בעקבי הצאן ורעי את גדיותיך״. אל תקרי ״גדיותיך״, אל", "context": "R. Eleazar b. R. Zadok recalls an impoverished woman gathering barley from between horses’ hooves at Acre. The horse supplies a concrete degradation/poverty setting.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Eleazar b. R. Zadok recalls an impoverished woman gathering barley from between horses’ hooves at Acre. The horse supplies a concrete degradation/poverty setting.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_hooves_poverty_image", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-ketubot-111b-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Ketubot", "locator": "111b:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot.111b.2", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Nashim/Ketubot/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "וכן אמרו: יצחק ושמעון ואושעיא אמרו דבר אחד: הלכה כרבי יהודה בפרדות. דתניא רבי יהודה אומר: פרדה שתבעה — אין מרביעין עליה לא סוס ולא חמור, אלא מינה.", "context": "R. Judah’s rule says a female mule in heat may be bred neither with a horse nor donkey unless with her own kind. Legal breeding classification, parallel to Chullin.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Judah’s rule says a female mule in heat may be bred neither with a horse nor donkey unless with her own kind. Legal breeding classification, parallel to Chullin.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "mule_breeding_rule_parallel", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-kiddushin-24b-10-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Kiddushin", "locator": "24b:10", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin.24b.10", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Nashim/Kiddushin/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "והתני רמי בר יחזקאל: תרנגול שהושיט ראשו לאויר כלי זכוכית, ותקע בו ושברו משלם נזק שלם. ואמר רב יוסף, אמרי בי רב: סוס שצנף וחמור שנער, ושברו כלים בתוך הבית – משלמים חצי נזק.", "context": "A horse neighing and breaking vessels indoors is assigned half damages. The passage concerns indirect damage by sound, not supernatural agency.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A horse neighing and breaking vessels indoors is assigned half damages. The passage concerns indirect damage by sound, not supernatural agency.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horse_sound_damage", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-menachot-85b-17-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Menachot", "locator": "85b:17", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot.85b.17", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Bavli/Seder%20Kodashim/Menachot/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "Sefaria merged Hebrew export (William Davidson witness family)", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "לאחר שאכלו ושתו, מדד לו שמן במאה ריבוא. אמר לו: כלום אתה צריך ליותר? אמר לו: הן, אלא שאין לי דמים. אמר לו: אם אתה רוצה ליקח – קח, ואני אלך עמך ואטול דמיו. מדד לו שמן בשמונה עשר ריבוא. אמרו: לא הניח או", "context": "A story of an enormous oil purchase says every available horse, mule, camel and donkey in the Land of Israel was hired for transport. Hyperbolic abundance/logistics imagery, not otherworldly travel.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A story of an enormous oil purchase says every available horse, mule, camel and donkey in the Land of Israel was hired for transport. Hyperbolic abundance/logistics imagery, not otherworldly travel.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["research-runner"], "task_id": "BAV-007", "role": "horses_in_mass_oil_transport", "limitations": ["Saved complete target segment from the BAV-002 primary export was read; live adjacent-segment API retrieval timed out, so no broader daf context is claimed in this pass.", "No manuscript or printed-edition collation, traditional commentary review, or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-11", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
